From: Piotr Kubik <piotr.kubik@adtran.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 13:50:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: reload a pending setup whose AP MLD goes away

When an MLD config update removes an AP MLD, mld_set_config()
reloads each interface that has a BSS of that MLD in hostapd.bss.
An interface whose setup is still pending has no BSS there yet, so it
keeps the removed MLD in its config. When the setup continues, it adds
a BSS for an MLD interface that no longer exists, and the add fails.

Reload a pending setup whose config holds a BSS of the removed MLD as
well, so that it starts again from the new MLD config.
---
--- a/openwrt/files/hostapd.uc
+++ b/openwrt/files/hostapd.uc
@@ -2435,6 +2435,14 @@ function mld_set_config(config)
 				continue;
 			reload_iface[iface] = true;
 		}
+
+		// A pending setup has no BSS in hostapd.bss yet, and adds the
+		// BSSes of its config after the MLD interface is gone.
+		for (let iface, pending in hostapd.data.pending_config) {
+			if (index(map(pending.config.bss, (b) => b.ifname), name) < 0)
+				continue;
+			reload_iface[iface] = true;
+		}
 	}
 
 	for (let name in reload_iface)
